# ChatWala'au line-ending policy
# ============================================================
# Scoped to this directory: the git repository root is the PARENT
# (C:\Apps\DevOps.WeDXcc), which holds unrelated sibling projects. A
# .gitattributes here applies to ChatWalaau/ and below, and to nothing else.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The project already declares LF in two places:
#
#   .editorconfig       end_of_line = lf     (for every file)
#   frontend/biome.jsonc "lineEnding": "lf"   (enforced by `pnpm run check`)
#
# Neither is visible to git. On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# (the Git for Windows default) git rewrites LF to CRLF on the way out, so a
# freshly cloned tree violates a rule the repository itself sets. The result
# was `pnpm run check` reporting 60 formatter errors against files that are
# byte-perfect in the repository -- the working copy was wrong, not the code.
#
# Declaring the policy here makes git honour what the project already says,
# for every contributor, on every platform, regardless of their local
# core.autocrlf setting. Nothing about file CONTENT changes: the blobs stored
# in git have always been LF.

# Default: treat as text, normalise to LF in the repository AND in the
# working tree. `text eol=lf` is deliberate over `text=auto` -- the latter
# still defers the working-tree ending to core.autocrlf on some git versions.
* text eol=lf

# ---- Binary: never touched, never diffed as text ----
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.pdf   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.exe   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# ---- Lockfiles: text, but noisy as diffs ----
pnpm-lock.yaml  text eol=lf -diff
uv.lock         text eol=lf -diff

# ---- Windows-only scripts, if any are ever added ----
# .bat / .cmd need CRLF; none are tracked today, but declaring it now means a
# future one cannot be silently broken by the LF default above.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
